<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- A tear-off calendar page reading "28", with two binder rings and a curled corner, after the
     reference the user supplied (2026-09-28) minus its tick. Everything sits inside the adaptive
     icon's 66dp safe circle (21..87), so no launcher mask clips it.

     The number is fixed: a launcher icon is a static resource, and only the system's own calendar
     gets a launcher hook to redraw today's date. -->
